// Odin bindings for the PS Vita user-mode SDK (VitaSDK, psp2/*.h and
// psp2common/*.h).
//
// Almost every file in this package is GENERATED by tools/bindgen/gen.py from
// the installed VitaSDK headers; those files start with a "GENERATED" line and
// must not be edited by hand (re-run the generator instead). The hand-written
// files are:
//
//   sce.odin      this file
//   inline.odin   ports of the headers' `static inline` functions and
//                 function-like macros, which have no symbol to bind
//   helpers.odin  small conveniences that are not in the SDK
//
// Naming:
//   functions   unchanged                 sceCtrlPeekBufferPositive
//   types       `Sce` prefix dropped      SceCtrlData        -> CtrlData
//   constants   `SCE_` prefix dropped     SCE_CTRL_CROSS     -> CTRL_CROSS
//   enums       Odin enums, common prefix dropped
//                                         SCE_TOUCH_SAMPLING_STATE_START
//                                           -> TouchSamplingState.START
//   bit flags and error codes are untyped constants (CTRL_CROSS,
//   CTRL_ERROR_INVALID_ARG), so they combine with `|` and compare directly
//   with the i32 a function returns.
//
// One file per header: psp2/ctrl.h -> ctrl.odin, psp2/kernel/threadmgr/mutex.h
// -> kernel_threadmgr_mutex.odin. A psp2common header shares the file of the
// psp2 header with the same path. Each file's header comment lists the stub
// libraries (-l flags) its functions need.
//
// ABI notes (see docs/getting-started.md):
//   - Functions with a float or double parameter or return value are bound
//     through lib/sce/bridge.c (generated). Add `sce` to BRIDGES in build.bat
//     when you use one of them.
//   - Every Odin enum here is 32 bits wide. VitaSDK's GCC makes enums as small
//     as their values allow, so a struct field whose C type is an enum is
//     written as u8/u16 where GCC stores it that way; the comment on the field
//     names the enum.
//   - Struct sizes are checked with #assert against the sizes GCC reports.
package sce
